  "notes": "Most children start Reception in the September of the school year they turn 5. Reception counts as compulsory school age in Jersey but sits in the Early Years Foundation Stage, so it is left out, as for England. The Jersey curriculum is based on England's national curriculum and key stages; most pupils take GCSEs in Years 10–11 and compulsory education ends at 16. Four non-fee-paying schools teach ages 11–16; the selective Hautlieu takes Years 10–13, with Year 12 (A level) places depending on GCSE results."
